WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.3 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Governance structures by legal form

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
You have governance from day one: decide who will direct and oversee, before you sign founding documents.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.133
Governance is how an organisation is directed and held to account. Management is how it is run day to day. You have some governance from day one, even if it is only how the founders decide.

4
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:29.133
Two jobs, often the same people

5
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:42.315
Governance: Asks: are we doing the right things, well and lawfully? Sets strategy, budget and key policies. For example: The two tutoring founders meet quarterly to approve the budget and choose a legal form.

6
00:00:42.315 --> 00:00:53.644
Management: Asks: are we doing things right, day to day? Runs plans, schedules and delivery. For example: The same founders set this week's tutoring timetable and book the room.

7
00:00:53.644 --> 00:01:06.915
Advisory group: Adds expertise and voice, but does not decide unless your documents give it that role. For example: Three parents and a retired teacher advise the tutoring service twice a year.

8
00:01:07.315 --> 00:01:07.915
Who governs, by legal form

9
00:01:07.915 --> 00:01:13.589
Nonprofit or charity: a board of trustees or directors, legally responsible.

10
00:01:13.589 --> 00:01:18.893
Company: directors appointed by shareholders, who keep certain key decisions.

11
00:01:18.893 --> 00:01:25.937
Cooperative: its members, who usually elect a committee to oversee the work.

12
00:01:26.337 --> 00:01:26.937
Why it matters early

13
00:01:26.937 --> 00:01:32.611
1. Your founding document fixes the rules, so decide before you sign.

14
00:01:32.611 --> 00:01:37.915
2. Clear roles stop founders confusing advice, oversight and daily decisions.

15
00:01:37.915 --> 00:01:44.219
3. Funders and partners trust organisations that are held to account.

16
00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:45.219
What it guides

17
00:01:45.219 --> 00:01:50.893
1. Your choice of legal form and the founding document you adopt.

18
00:01:50.893 --> 00:01:56.196
2. Your reserved matters and governance calendar, in the next lesson.

19
00:01:56.196 --> 00:02:03.241
3. Who you invite first: advisers now, a fuller board as you grow.

20
00:02:03.641 --> 00:02:04.241
What to avoid

21
00:02:04.241 --> 00:02:09.915
Signing founding documents before deciding how you want to be governed.

22
00:02:09.915 --> 00:02:15.219
Treating an advisory group as if it carried legal responsibility.

23
00:02:15.219 --> 00:02:21.893
Skipping local rules: ask someone with a legal background before registering.

24
00:02:22.493 --> 00:02:24.293
You describe the governance your form requires and the one you want.

25
00:02:24.293 --> 00:02:28.293
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

26
00:02:29.793 --> 00:02:32.893
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
